# Frozen THIRD-PARTY DOCKER DEPENDENCY versions - base images and external
# binaries baked into the LiveReview Docker image (Dockerfile and
# Dockerfile.crosscompile). NOT the LiveReview application version (that's
# tracked separately by `scripts/lrops.py version`/`make version` and Git
# tags) - this file only pins the *ingredients* of the Docker image itself:
# node/golang/debian base images, dbmate, River CLI/UI, vl-convert,
# codebase-memory-mcp, dbctx, AgentLaws.
#
# Bump a version here, not in the Dockerfiles. scripts/lrops.py reads this
# file and injects each entry as a `--build-arg` for every docker/buildx
# build (single-arch and multiarch alike), and both Dockerfiles declare a
# matching `ARG ... ` with the same name so the value actually takes effect.
#
# RIVER_VERSION (the `river` CLI) must match the `github.com/riverqueue/river`
# version pinned in go.mod, so the CLI matches the library compiled into the
# main binary. Check go.mod when bumping this.
#
# RIVERUI_VERSION is a SEPARATE, independently-released tool (a standalone
# HTTP server, not linked into the main binary) and is free to depend on a
# different underlying river version than RIVER_VERSION/go.mod - do not try
# to keep it in lockstep. Both Dockerfiles build river and riverui in two
# SEPARATE temp Go modules specifically so each one's dependency graph
# resolves independently; if a future edit combines them back into one
# shared `go mod init` + multiple `go get`s, Go's version-selection can
# silently pick an incompatible mix of their shared transitive deps and
# break the build with confusing errors deep in an unrelated package. Keep
# them isolated.
#
# Checking for updates / bumping versions: see docker/DOCKER-DEPS.md, or run
# `make check-docker-deps` / `make update-docker-deps` / `make update-docker-deps-yes`.
#
# LOCKING a dependency so it is never touched by `make update-docker-deps` /
# `make update-docker-deps-yes` (or the automatic pre-build check): add its
# KEY to PINNED_DOCKER_DEPS below (comma-separated). It still gets checked
# and reported (so you can see when a locked dependency falls behind), it
# just won't be offered or auto-applied. Remove it from the list to unlock,
# or pass --include-pinned to scripts/check_docker_deps.py for a one-off
# override. Always keep this line present, even when empty.
PINNED_DOCKER_DEPS=

# Base images
NODE_IMAGE_TAG=20.20.2-alpine
GOLANG_IMAGE_TAG=1.26.8-bookworm
DEBIAN_IMAGE_TAG=trixie-20260824-slim

# Go-installed tools
RIVER_VERSION=v0.32.0
RIVERUI_VERSION=v0.19.0

# GitHub-release binaries
DBMATE_VERSION=v2.35.1
VLCONVERT_VERSION=v1.9.0
CODEBASE_MEMORY_MCP_VERSION=v0.10.8
DBCTX_VERSION=v0.1.0
ALAWS_VERSION=v0.1.0
